Package: hrsim
Type: Package
Title: Simulation Engine for 'Unstable Heteroresistance as a Stepping
    Stone to Stable Resistance via Compensatory Mutations'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Brandon A.", "Berryhill", email = "Brandon.Berryhill@imbim.uu.se",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Brandon A. Berryhill <Brandon.Berryhill@imbim.uu.se>
Description: Compiled (C++, via 'Rcpp') simulation engine for the model of
    heteroresistance with compensatory mutations in Berryhill and Andersson
    (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.10.08.756632>, "Unstable Heteroresistance as a
    Stepping Stone to Stable Resistance via Compensatory Mutations". The
    model follows twenty bacterial states, a limiting resource, an antibiotic
    and beta-lactamase under serial transfer, by fixed-step Euler integration
    with a Monte Carlo transition layer. simulate_hr() runs one replicate,
    run_sim() takes the named arguments of the R reference engine and
    calls simulate_hr() with the unpacked vectors and scalars, and
    debug_step1() and debug_step1_fired() expose the first step to the
    package's tests. Each call runs one replicate on one thread. The C++
    source was translated from the R reference implementation with the
    assistance of a generative AI model (Claude Opus 4.8, Anthropic) and was
    verified against that reference before any results were generated from
    it, as described in the Methods of the paper.
